<p>Scientific software serves people with different questions, skills, and working environments. Understanding those differences gives teams a starting point for improving the tools researchers rely on.</p>

<p>The UX in Science hub offers a place to explore that work. Its resource pages cover user research, design, and engineering, while the communities page points to groups where people can exchange experiences and learn from one another.</p>

<h2>Connect practice with community</h2>
<p>Useful conversations often begin with a specific question: where does a workflow become confusing, what information is missing, or which task takes more effort than it should? Sharing those questions can help people find relevant methods and others working through similar challenges.</p>

